# Flipbook page curl

The page curl is a finished, book-agnostic reader feature. Keep it. Do not replace it with CSS shapes, SVG folds, or a new asset unless the user supplies one.

- Asset: `media/images/page-curl.png` (transparent flap). Do not rotate it.
- Markup: `.page-curl` is a sibling of `main` (not inside it — `rebuild()` wipes main).
- Geometry lives in CSS variables on `.page-curl`. Tune those tokens only; do not re-measure each page.
- Show on every page that has a following page. Hide on THE END.
- Peek is the next distinct illustration (`object-fit: cover; object-position: top right`), not a 1:1 crop of the page corner.
- Paper tint is the cream `--page-paper` filter on `.page-curl-flap`.
- Arrive with the turn (`updateCurl(destination)` at flip start). Do not hide the curl while `busy`.
